01:35:46.040 --> 01:35:48.210
like 15 people in the last 30 years

2162
01:35:48.210 --> 01:35:49.537
have finished this thing?

2163
01:35:49.537 --> 01:35:50.422
It's incredible.
What is the deal?

2164
01:35:50.422 --> 01:35:51.913
Since 1986.

2165
01:35:51.913 --> 01:35:53.740
So why is it so hard?

2166
01:35:53.740 --> 01:35:58.210
Lazarus has created the most incredibly difficult race

2167
01:35:58.210 --> 01:36:00.703
you can imagine, for number of reasons.

2168
01:36:02.600 --> 01:36:04.310
It has 120 miles.

2169
01:36:04.310 --> 01:36:06.900
Like that's not that big of a deal,

2170
01:36:06.900 --> 01:36:10.450
but the fact that it's got-

2171
01:36:10.450 --> 01:36:12.348
It's all relative.

2172
01:36:12.348 --> 01:36:13.181
All relative, yeah.

2173
01:36:13.181 --> 01:36:14.560
You just ran 354 miles.

2174
01:36:14.560 --> 01:36:15.573
So like 120.

2175
01:36:17.246 --> 01:36:18.570
It's supposed to be a hundred,

2176
01:36:18.570 --> 01:36:20.380
but really it's like ends up being 120,

2177
01:36:20.380 --> 01:36:21.890
because you have to navigate.

2178
01:36:21.890 --> 01:36:25.893
So only 20% is on trail and 80% is off trail.

2179
01:36:26.839 --> 01:36:28.210
So that extra 20 is built in

2180
01:36:28.210 --> 01:36:30.330
because you know you're gonna go off

2181
01:36:30.330 --> 01:36:31.163
the course and stuff?

2182
01:36:31.163 --> 01:36:33.100
Yeah, everybody knows that it's longer than a hundred.

2183
01:36:33.100 --> 01:36:34.950
So you just want to think already,

2184
01:36:34.950 --> 01:36:37.970
like you said, you don't prepare yourself

2185
01:36:37.970 --> 01:36:39.370
for what it's gonna be.

2186
01:36:39.370 --> 01:36:42.910
Then you got close to 60,000 feet of elevation climbing.

2187
01:36:42.910 --> 01:36:47.160
So that's like two times up Mount Everest and back down

2188
01:36:47.160 --> 01:36:48.930
in 60 hours.

2189
01:36:48.930 --> 01:36:53.280
And then you have going in the fog at nighttime.

2190
01:36:53.280 --> 01:36:56.060
Imagine you're off course or you're on a course,

2191
01:36:56.060 --> 01:36:59.615
that's off trail and it's pitch-black,

2192
01:36:59.615 --> 01:37:03.724
it's gonna be maybe a quarter moon, there's fog.

2193
01:37:03.724 --> 01:37:08.600
You basically are relying on somewhat intuition,

2194
01:37:08.600 --> 01:37:11.040
somewhat on your compass.

2195
01:37:11.040 --> 01:37:12.720
I'm carrying that with me now all the time. (chuckles)

2196
01:37:12.720 --> 01:37:14.097
Orienteering kind of thing.

2197
01:37:14.097 --> 01:37:16.040
Little bit orienteering.

2198
01:37:16.040 --> 01:37:19.597
And then not only that, you have to follow Laz's riddles

2199
01:37:22.840 --> 01:37:24.890
that he has written in his own language

2200
01:37:25.862 --> 01:37:27.280
to where these books are hidden.

2201
01:37:27.280 --> 01:37:28.940
And so there's 14 books shift.

2202
01:37:28.940 --> 01:37:30.560
You have to find find the one

2203
01:37:30.560 --> 01:37:33.380
that's maybe at the state penitentiary,

2204
01:37:33.380 --> 01:37:35.531
that they have there.

2205
01:37:35.531 --> 01:37:36.980
You have to find one underneath a rock

2206
01:37:36.980 --> 01:37:38.740
that's by the Birch tree.

2207
01:37:38.740 --> 01:37:41.440
It's very encryptic.

2208
01:37:41.440 --> 01:37:44.900
So it's a challenge once you get like yourself to a place

2209
01:37:44.900 --> 01:37:47.050
where you've been going for 36 hours

2210
01:37:48.630 --> 01:37:52.480
and you have to navigate at nighttime and you're tired,

2211
01:37:52.480 --> 01:37:54.220
you've had sleep deprivation.

2212
01:37:54.220 --> 01:37:56.580
Most people don't sleep even the night before the race,

2213
01:37:56.580 --> 01:37:58.700
'cause they're waiting for the conch shell to be blown

2214
01:37:58.700 --> 01:38:01.603
and they're like have a hard time falling asleep.

2215
01:38:03.546 --> 01:38:06.770
So it becomes really important

2216
01:38:06.770 --> 01:38:10.390
