01:38:26.100 --> 01:38:30.140
Imagine climbing up and down Everest in 60 hours

2223
01:38:30.140 --> 01:38:34.090
and it's not like on a road or like a path

2224
01:38:34.090 --> 01:38:38.720
it's on like this muddy climb,

2225
01:38:38.720 --> 01:38:41.833
up like a steep embankment with thorns.

2226
01:38:42.714 --> 01:38:44.540
It's very challenging,

2227
01:38:44.540 --> 01:38:46.481
but that's what I love about it.

2228
01:38:46.481 --> 01:38:49.750
So how do you get your head around that

2229
01:38:49.750 --> 01:38:53.270
and sort of customize your training

2230
01:38:53.270 --> 01:38:57.560
to be in the best kind of prepared state that you can.

2231
01:38:57.560 --> 01:39:00.650
Yeah, that's what I love about taking on

2232
01:39:00.650 --> 01:39:01.660
these new challenges.

2233
